# Revising against feedback

You are not starting from a blank page. The current committed draft is
below, along with feedback on it. This is a **surgical modification**,
not a redesign: your job is to make the changes the feedback actually
asks for and emit the full body back, verbatim, everywhere the
feedback is silent. Sections the feedback doesn't mention are sticky —
copy them forward unchanged rather than re-deriving them, even if you
would have written them differently from scratch. Re-deriving
untouched sections is how a small, targeted fix turns into an
unreviewable full rewrite three regenerations later.

